  "approach": "Implement an HTTP server using Python's http.server module with a custom request handler. Route requests based on HTTP method and path (/tasks, /tasks/{id}). Use a dictionary for in-memory storage with auto-incrementing IDs. Validate inputs for required fields and predefined status values ('pendiente', 'en progreso', 'completada'). Set Content-Type: application/json for all responses and return appropriate HTTP status codes (200, 201, 204, 400, 404). Handle errors with JSON messages for undefined routes or invalid requests.",
